# dashcam-exporter — personal settings
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in your own values.
# These are kept OUT of config.txt on purpose: config.txt is committed, and your
# home location should not be. A real environment variable of the same name
# overrides the value here.
#
# HOME LOCATION (optional but recommended).
# If set, the car parking within SET_HOME_RADIUS_M metres of this point is a
# hard trip boundary: arriving home ends a trip, and the next departure from
# home starts a new one — even when the trip's own GPS anchor is unreliable
# (e.g. loop-recording overwrote the departure, so the footage starts already
# out on the road). Grab the coordinates from Google Maps: right-click your
# home -> the first line of the menu is "lat, lon"; paste them here.
#
# The values below are a PLACEHOLDER (roughly central Metro Manila) — replace
# them with your own.
SET_HOME_LAT=14.5000
SET_HOME_LON=121.0000

# Radius in metres counted as "at home". Default 100 if unset.
SET_HOME_RADIUS_M=100

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLISHING — only if you have somewhere to publish to.
#
# ONE setting: the plugin that does it, as
# "<path to a .py>:<BuilderClass>:<UploaderClass>". One file, two classes — the
# builder is item 6, the uploader is item 7 — and where they send things (a
# bucket, a server, an external disk, a folder) is their business, not this
# repo's. That is why there is one key here and not four naming a destination.
#
# It is a path to YOUR file, which is as personal as the coordinates above and
# is why it lives here rather than in config.txt: config.txt is tracked, so a
# value put there gets committed and pushed.
#
# Leave it unset and the CLI is import -> render -> local page; item 7 greys
# out with a reason instead of disappearing. Set it to something that will not
# load and the tool STOPS, loudly — it never falls back to the local edition,
# because a menu that has quietly stopped publishing looks exactly like one
# that is publishing fine.
#
# examples/local_website.py is a complete working plugin to copy.
#
# A real environment variable of the same name overrides this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#SET_UPLOAD_PLUGIN=~/dev/dashcam-exporter/examples/local_website.py:LocalWebSiteBuilderPlugin:LocalWebSiteUploader

# Where the footage comes from. Any directory holding a DCIM tree: a mounted
# card, a copy of one on an external disk, a folder someone handed you.
#SET_CARD=/Volumes/NO NAME
